    "1.4.11.7.5730": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.5730\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [BETA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: July 25, 2026\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nRELEASE NOTE: The original release changelog describes this snapshot as stable relative to earlier snapshots. This is a historical release note, not a guarantee of stability for every modpack.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nRELEASE STATUS AND REQUIREMENTS\n- The original July 2026 release notes identify this as the most stable 1.4.11.8 snapshot at the time and recommend upgrading to it or a later snapshot.\n- Forge 1.20.1: 47.2.0 or higher. Required: GeckoLib 4.4.2 or higher. Recommended: JEI 15.3.0.8 or higher.\n\nMAJOR BUG FIXES\n- Fixed the AATST integrated-server tick-freeze issue by redesigning applier/queuer coordination.\n- Fixed the Rock Salt custom loot-table drop error.\n\nWORLD GENERATION AND BLOCKS\n- Expanded Rock Salt generation to Deep Ocean and Deep Lukewarm Ocean biomes and allowed Clay replacement.\n- Changed Rock Salt generation shape from Uniform to Triangle.\n- Increased Rock Salt generation averages from 5 to 7 per chunk and 8 to 10 per group.\n- Expanded Rock Salt generation height from Y 45-60 to Y 40-62 and adjusted its harvest-tool tier.\n- Adjusted Rain Collector's preferred tool for breaking.\n- Updated Y-axis rotation of Medical Cabinet, Rain Collector, and Elemental Block; adjusted Medical Cabinet block faces.\n\nENCHANTMENTS AND STATUS EFFECTS\n- Made Nether Heatness Immunity inapplicable to Netherite Armor and changed its rarity from Rare to Uncommon.\n- Expanded Awake Elapsed System (ALS) with Fatigue Level 3 and localized Fatigue Levels 2/3 alerts.\n- Updated sleeping's ALS reduction from one day to one day and eight hours, with smarter subtraction and day handling.\n\nCOMMANDS AND FEEDBACK\n- Enhanced ALS get/set/reset command messages with formatting, pluralization, and revised wording.\n- Refined Special Book set/get/reset command messages and syntax for Book of Inspiration, Restless, Physician, and Hearty.\n- Added decimal-value validation, smarter override checks, formatted messages, and literal reset parameters for Special Book commands.\n- Added an advanced smart spawn-position checker to the /RW zombified-entity easy wave.\n- Improved /RW success and failure messages for difficulty, monster caps, and cooldowns.\n\nLOCALIZATION AND QUALITY OF LIFE\n- Improved gamerule names/descriptions for Starter Items Pack, Spawn Champions, Biome Temperatures, Player Elemental Invulnerability, Player Thirst Bar, Natural Water Source Penalties, and Medicine Apply Delay.\n- Updated Glacial, Freezing Cold, Cold, Hot, Very Hot, Scorching Hot, Scalding Hot, and Boiling Hot temperature-alert localization.\n- Polished descriptions for many advancements covering elemental crafting, weapons, upgrades, exploration, champions, medicine, and collections.\n- Updated advancement recipe rewards for First Fire Element and Ice Upgrade II.\n- Updated Electro's PowerCraft description/credits and added Spider Bite subtitle localization.\n\nTECHNICAL IMPROVEMENTS\n- Added the AATST Queuer procedure; made AATST Applier and Queuer client-side aware with safer per-entity coordination.\n- Updated Awake Elapsed System time subtraction and feedback handling.",
    "1.4.11.7.5080": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.5080\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: June 23, 2026\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nSTABILITY WARNING\nThe original release notes mark this snapshot as unstable, particularly for heavily modded worlds or servers. They warn about possible world-loading or server problems and suggest 1.4.11.7.1890 or 1.4.11.7.1620 as alternatives if problems occur. Back up your world before updating.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Added an expanded Confusion effect with special potions, twisted mushrooms, and custom behavior for players and mobs.\n- Added the First Aid Kit, placeable guide/special books, and improved Knife attacks.\n- Updated Elemental Army mob classes, AI, natural spawning, and integration with the Elemental Enforcement Addon.\n- Made falling-related leg penalties less severe.\n\nMAJOR BUG FIXES\n- Fixed the Freezing Status Effect attribute system.\n- Fixed Powered Electric Soldier PSCT/Powered Sword Countdown Timer behavior and health conditions for charged attacks.\n- Fixed some nighttime spawn-brightness checks and Elemental Enforcement Addon mod-ID/targeter conditions.\n\nITEMS, POTIONS, RECIPES, AND PLANTS\n- Added First Aid Kit, including use procedures and Medical Villager trade availability.\n- Added Potion of Confusion, Prolonged Confusion, Compulsive Confusion, Charged Confusion, and Charged Prolonged Confusion, with recipes.\n- Added Twisted Mushroom Plant and Charged Twisted Mushroom Plant, including generation and particle effects.\n- Enabled Electro's Guide, Melee Training Book, and Special Books to be placed on bookshelves via book tags.\n- Updated Knife texture, description, and bleeding attack behavior.\n- Updated Cotton Plant texture and adjusted the hunger effect from eating Infected Spider Eye.\n- Updated Medical Villager trades: Herbal Antibiotics quantity 3 to 5 and Antibiotics quantity 10 to 7.\n\nCONFUSION GAMEPLAY\n- Added the Confusion status effect and description.\n- Added player inverted movement controls, random hand/head movement, and Confused question-mark particles.\n- Added Confusion behavior for entities that may target nearby mobs, including their own species; added random panic wandering and no-target outcomes.\n- Added Confusion Level II random target selection, proximity swings, and cooldown logic.\n- Added special confused-Skeleton behavior: shaking, wobbling, sidesteps, panic dashes, health scaling, and limited self-attacks.\n- Added confused-Creeper behaviors involving false ignition, short panic fuses, rare explosions, and associated particles.\n- Added Confusion self-attack/panic-swing damage types and death messages.\n- Prevented some confusion targeting behavior when Unnoticeable is active.\n- Added player movement keybinds and supporting pressed/released handlers for forward, backward, left, and right.\n\nPARTICLES AND KNIFE COMBAT\n- Added Blood Drop, Confused (Question Mark), and Small/Medium Gentle Spore Drift particles.\n- Updated Knife attacks with advanced random effect chances, Bleed Resistance detection, blood-drop positioning, spawn-rate timing, and element tags.\n- Added Knife-attack immunity conditions for Cracker's Wither Storm mobs.\n- Added bleeding-particle worker procedures for players and entities.\n\nFREEZING, MEDICAL, AND FALLING SYSTEMS\n- Updated Freezing applied/expiry logic, replaced FEGT tracking with FMAW logic, and made freezing prevent sprinting.\n- Removed the extra Slowness effect from Ice Element Attacks.\n- Updated BLFA fall-injury distances for Sprained Leg, Splinted Leg, and Broken Leg; added Goat immunity.\n- Corrected Herobrine Level 30's reinforcement notification.\n\nELEMENTAL ARMY AND AI\n- Changed Electric/Ice Soldiers Levels 1-2, Ice Ranged Soldiers Levels 1-2, Powered Electric Soldier Level 3, Electro Levels 1/5/10, and Ice Level 1 to Neutral Mob classes with advanced spawning conditions.\n- Changed Electric and Ice Soldier Level 1 trainers to Pathfinder Mob classes.\n- Adjusted movement speeds for Electro, Ice, and selected Soldiers; reduced Electro Level 1/5/10 attributes.\n- Increased Ice Ranged Soldier Level 1/2 arrow attack delays.\n- Integrated Elemental Enforcement Addon anger-retaliation conditions across supported units; added ranged-retaliation safeguards and corrected targeter overrides for ranged soldiers.\n- Updated mob tags (including Zombie, Undead, Skeleton, Boss, and elemental unit tags) and confusion damage localization.",
    "1.4.11.7.3590": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.3590\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: July 25, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nSTABILITY WARNING\nThe original release notes mark this snapshot as unstable, particularly for heavily modded worlds or servers. They warn about possible world-loading or server problems and suggest 1.4.11.7.1890 or 1.4.11.7.1620 as alternatives if problems occur. Back up your world before updating.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Reintroduced the Rain Collector with water-collection mechanics and JEI integration.\n- Added Book of Hearty and the revamped 'Restful Vibes' music.\n\nBUG FIXES\n- Fixed the Rain Collector.\n- Corrected Berserk attack behavior for Ice Ranged Soldier Level 2.\n\nBLOCKS, ITEMS, AND RECIPES\n- Readded the Rain Collector block.\n- Added Book of Hearty (Special Book), Water Collector Grate, and Copper Rain Gatherer.\n- Added recipes for Rain Collector, Water Collector Grate, and Copper Rain Gatherer.\n- Updated the Sewing Kit recipe to use an Iron Nugget instead of an Iron Ingot.\n- Added Rain Collector-related recipe unlockers.\n\nRAIN COLLECTOR AND JEI\n- Enabled Rain Collector automatic ticking and NBT-based water storage, including maxWaterValue.\n- Added water-delivery procedures, GUI input/output slots, and Rain Gatherer modification support.\n- Added Rain Collector JEI recipe GUI, filtered-water recipes, and JEI information.\n- Updated the Filtered Water Bottle texture.\n\nSPECIAL BOOKS, STATUS EFFECTS, AND GAMEPLAY\n- Added Book of Hearty GUI, skill-level logic, health application, and set/get/reset Special Book commands.\n- Integrated Book of Hearty into starter respawn effects and Reset-All Special Book commands.\n- Increased Bowl of Rice water replenishment from 0.5 to 1.5.\n- Lowered hunger depletion from Mild, Active, and Advanced Decay.\n- Added Fury potency scaling to hunger drain and improved Berserk damage/source targeting.\n- Disabled shaking for Zombified Electric Soldier Level 4.\n- Updated Medical Villager trade multipliers for Sewing Kit and Splint.\n- Updated Radiated Flesh after-use effects and Food Poisoning localization.\n\nMUSIC AND LANGUAGES\n- Added ElectroGaming10 - Restful Vibes - Remake, replacing the older track in Survival Autoplay Music.\n- Updated Japanese, German, Filipino, Chinese (Taiwan), Spanish (Mexico/Spain), and French.\n- Added English (Canada) translation support.",
    "1.4.11.7.3000": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.3000\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: March 14, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nSTABILITY WARNING\nThe original release notes mark this snapshot as unstable, particularly for heavily modded worlds or servers. They warn about possible world-loading or server problems and suggest 1.4.11.7.1890 or 1.4.11.7.1620 as alternatives if problems occur. Back up your world before updating.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Improved effect descriptions across a wide range of medical and gameplay status effects.\n- Expanded player HUD and localization support.\n\nSTATUS EFFECTS AND MEDICAL ITEMS\n- Revised descriptions for Broken Leg, Sprained Leg, Splinted Leg, Concussion, Deep Laceration, Abrasion, and Treated Abrasion.\n- Revised descriptions for Inspiration, Quenched, Mild/Active/Advanced Decay, Bleeding, Shocked, Unnoticeable, and Freezing.\n- Set the Medicine Delay effect classification to neutral.\n- Improved Splinted Leg application notifications.\n- Fixed First Aid Bandage application in Creative Mode.\n- First Aid Bandage now applies Treated Abrasion only when Abrasion is present.\n\nHUD AND TEXT\n- Added Absorption HUD support through PBER player procedures, including the IceGamer1159/Arata PBER system entry.\n- Added the Food Poisoning localization key for the Radiated Flesh after-use behavior.\n\nLANGUAGES\n- Updated Japanese, Chinese (Taiwan), Filipino (Philippines), Spanish (Mexico), Spanish (Spain), French (France), and German (Germany).\n\nDEVELOPMENT NOTE\n- The original public changelog states that some additional changes were kept hidden; this entry does not speculate about those changes.",
    "1.4.11.7.2610": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.2610\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: March 8, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nSTABILITY WARNING\nThe original release notes mark this snapshot as unstable, particularly for heavily modded worlds or servers. They warn about possible world-loading or server problems and suggest 1.4.11.7.1890 or 1.4.11.7.1620 as alternatives if problems occur. Back up your world before updating.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Added the Book of Physician, Bleed Resistance, and Treated Abrasion.\n- Expanded first-aid interactions and redesigned the player Bossbar/HUD behavior.\n\nBUG FIXES\n- Fixed the Zombified Creeper's Unnoticeable-entity fuse behavior.\n- Fixed Honey Bottle's interaction with the Medicine Apply Delay gamerule.\n- Fixed the player-punch Hit SFX.\n- Fixed the Dead HUD behavior in PBER.\n\nITEMS, BOOKS, AND STATUS EFFECTS\n- Added Book of Physician (Special Book), its GUI, skill system, and Special Book command support.\n- Added Bleed Resistance and Treated Abrasion status effects and Bleed Resistance description.\n- Added Bleed Resistance handling to Band-Aid, First Aid Bandage, and Sewing Kit.\n- Updated Deep Laceration to detect Bleed Resistance; revised effect icon and application notices.\n- Splint now interacts with the Book of Physician system, can cure Sprained Leg, and heals Broken Leg faster when applied.\n- Added Treated Abrasion application through First Aid Bandage and additional Abrasion detectors/attack handling.\n- Updated Bleeding and Splinted Leg status classifications, the Bleeding overlay position, and Concussion Resistance description.\n\nPLAYER HUD AND GAMEPLAY\n- Improved Bossbar Executable, including entity targeting, per-player Bossbars, automatic hiding, and HUD color.\n- Added PBER (player Bossbar) procedures, Absorption HUD, and an absorption scoreboard runner.\n- Adjusted Fatigue effect damage and infection-particle placement for players.\n- Added food replenishment for Jellies and excluded them from the food drainer.\n- Added Zombified Creeper avoidance behavior for Cats and Ocelots, Zombified Skeleton avoidance for Wolves, and a Wolf targeter for Zombified Skeleton.\n- Refined Reinforcement Wave zombified-entity command logic and Melee Training Book battle procedures.\n- Added Book of Physician to Librarian trades and lowered Book of Inspiration's emerald price.\n\nTECHNICAL CHANGES\n- Expanded MADG variables and join, leave, sleep, respawn, and command checkers.\n- Added TBCD variable/counter and TADA, TAET, and TAEL variable systems.\n- Integrated TAET/TAEL with NCEG and EVC systems.",
    "1.4.11.7.2000": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.2000\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: January 17, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nSTABILITY WARNING\nThe original release notes mark this snapshot as unstable, particularly for heavily modded worlds or servers. They warn about possible world-loading or server problems and suggest 1.4.11.7.1890 or 1.4.11.7.1620 as alternatives if problems occur. Back up your world before updating.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nRELEASE NOTE\n- The original 1.4.11.7.2000 changelog also reproduces the 1.4.11.7.1890 notes (including Baked Apple, HUD improvements, the Effect Attribute Giver fix, and combat balancing).\n- The changes below are specifically listed under 1.4.11.7.2000, so the earlier release's changes are not repeated in full.\n\nGAMEPLAY AND ENTITIES\n- Added Apple Pie to food replenishment and the food-drainer exclusion list.\n- Expanded the Attack Sickened Mobs system to trainers.\n- Adjusted Zombified Skeleton ranged-attack timing.\n- Updated the Elemental Hunter advancement to include infected monster parts.\n\nVISUALS AND UI\n- Removed glow textures from Electric Swords I-III, Electric Pickaxe I, Ice Swords I-II, and Jackson's Axe I.\n- Modified Bossbar Executable.\n- Updated the Fruits tag to include Baked Apple.\n\nMEDICINE AND TECHNICAL SYSTEMS\n- Integrated the MADG variable into Herbal Antibiotics, Antibiotics, and Painkillers.\n- Added the MADG Variable System and MADG Counter.",
    "1.4.11.7.1890": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.1890\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: January 12, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Added Baked Apple and its smelting recipe.\n- Expanded Bossbar HUD conditions and modified Electro's PowerCraft client music configuration.\n- Rebalanced several melee weapons and refined status effects.\n\nMAJOR BUG FIX\n- Fixed the Effect Attribute Giver system.\n\nFOOD AND RECIPES\n- Added Baked Apple and the Baked Apple smelting recipe/unlocker.\n- Added Baked Apple to the food replenisher, food-drainer exclusions, and Fruits tag.\n\nHUD AND INTERFACES\n- Improved Bossbar displays for Bleeding, death, low health, non-full health, reduced health, and extended health.\n- Added player-detection visibility handling to Bossbar Executable.\n- Improved localization for Element Invulnerability, Sewing Kit application errors, and Sprained Leg descriptions.\n\nGAMEPLAY AND ENTITY BALANCE\n- Added sickened-mob detection to the Zombie Attack system.\n- Removed Crimson Forest spawning for Powerful Creeper Levels I and II.\n- Expanded BLFA immunities for Magma Cubes, Slimes, and Frogs and lowered its penalty timer.\n- Added Netherite Armor immunity to the Boiling Hot effect; adjusted Boiling Hot and NHTD timer behavior.\n- Added a not-riding check to the Thirst Bar condition.\n- Reduced efficiency/attack speed for Electric Swords I-III and efficiency for Jackson's Axe I.\n- Adjusted Zombified Skeleton ranged-attack arrows.\n- Added FADA logic to Fatigue; Fatigue can now reduce maximum health.\n\nMUSIC AND TECHNICAL CHANGES\n- Added EPC Client Configuration music checks to Electro's Melee Training Book and Herobrine Reinforcement playback.\n- Updated the Jackson's Axe element tag and Effect Attribute Giver.\n- Added the FADA Variable System.\n\nVERSION NOTE\n- The original release notes recommend this version for heavily modded setups encountering issues with 1.4.11.7.2000.",
    "1.4.11.7.1620": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.1620\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: January 9, 2025\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nMAJOR BUG FIX\n- Fixed the Concussion Attribute Giver system's attack-damage handling.\n\nZOMBIE INFECTION AND ENTITIES\n- Added or adjusted infection particles and display names for affected players and Mild Decay entities.\n- Updated player infection blacklists for zombified entities and zombie-tagged mobs.\n- Adjusted Ice Soldier infection particles and Jackson Zombiez Level 1 AI.\n- Updated Zombified Skeleton Level 2 entity base and AI tasks.\n- Expanded monster-in-range (MIR) detection and added an Attack Sickened Mobs system.\n\nSTATUS EFFECTS AND GAMEPLAY\n- Updated Medicine Delay interactions with Concussion Resistance and Concussion's attack-damage attribute handling.\n- Added Cat immunity to the BLFA system.\n- Integrated SPLDA and SPLSS variables with Splinted Leg, SLSS with Sprained Leg, and BLSS with Broken Leg.\n- Revised armor-driven temperature changes in the TBH Temperature Controller.\n- Changed the Bleeding effect color and adjusted spawning difficulty scaling.\n\nTECHNICAL CHANGES\n- Added MIR Detector and variable logic.\n- Added AATST variable, counter, and applier systems.\n- Added element tags for Jackson's Axe, Electric Pickaxe, Electric Sword III, Jackson entities, and Electric Soldier Levels 1 and 2.\n- Updated the Electric Soldier Level 1 tag to include its trainer.",
    "1.4.11.7.1420": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.1420\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: December 25, 2024\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Introduced the Electro's PowerCraft Client Configuration System.\n- Added /SB (Special Book) and /RW (Reinforcement Wave) commands.\n- Expanded the Zombie Infection system with new infection particles, sounds, targets, and immunity rules.\n\nCOMMANDS AND CONFIGURATION\n- Added Special Book commands to set, get, and reset Book of Inspiration and Book of Restless levels; added a reset-all option.\n- Added the Reinforcement Wave command, initially supporting an easy wave of zombified entities.\n- Improved Reinforcement Wave behavior with cooldown (RWCD), difficulty detection, ECD integration, and spread-out spawning.\n- Added a client option to control playback of the Electro's PowerCraft soundtrack (Play_EPCOST), connected to ambient, startup, and survival music routines.\n- Added a Play_OOST option for other soundtracks; the original notes mark this option as not yet functional.\n\nZOMBIE INFECTION AND DECAY\n- Added the Infection particle and expanded its use with animals, vanilla mobs, players, Electro, Electric Soldiers, Powered Electric Soldiers, and Ice Soldiers.\n- Added infection sounds for multiple Electro, Electric Soldier, Powered Electric Soldier, and Ice Soldier variants.\n- Added zombie-infection scripts for Ice Soldier Level 1 and its trainer; expanded vanilla infection support to Villagers.\n- Added Piglin, Skeleton, Spider, and Creeper handling in the Mild Decay infection system.\n- Expanded Mild, Active, and Advanced Decay immunity rules for Zombified Skeleton, Spider, Creeper, undead entities, and zombie-tagged mobs.\n- Improved player infection display names and player infection handling through SIPC and its resetter system.\n\nGAMEPLAY AND BALANCE\n- Sewing Kit now cures Bleeding.\n- Adjusted the Zombified Creeper explosion range.\n- Lowered the emerald cost of elemental swords in Elemental Villager trades.\n- Electric Source, Electric Power, Energetic Electric Power, and Thunder Power are no longer fire-resistant; adjusted their item-destruction properties.\n- Added the ADR (Attribute Detection Remover) to Freezing, Broken Leg, and Sprained Leg effects.\n- Improved Inspiration regeneration at level I and added level II regeneration.\n- Updated Zombified Powered Electric Soldier targeting to include Ice.\n\nOTHER MODIFICATIONS\n- Updated Hit SFX, including the Spider Bite sound category.\n- Updated several electric and ice item file names.\n- Updated Medic advancement text, Wendigo loot, and Herobrine levels 15, 30, and 45.\n- Added elemental source/power tags for electric, ice, and fire items.\n\nBUG FIXES\n- Fixed excessive Zombified Human spawning when a player was killed by Mild Decay.",
    "1.4.11.7.800": "Electro's PowerCraft 1.4.11.7.800\nMinecraft 1.20.1 | Release Notes\n\n----------------------------------------\nRELEASE CHANNEL: [ALPHA] [1.4.11.8 SNAPSHOT]\nRELEASE DATE: December 20, 2024\n----------------------------------------\nThe Realistic Update | 1.4.11.8 Snapshot\n\nIMPORTANT COMPATIBILITY NOTICE\nVersions 1.4.11+ use mod ID electros_powercraft instead of electros_mod. Updating a world from 1.4.10.x or earlier can cause existing mod blocks and items to disappear. Back up the world before changing versions.\nStarter Pack notice: Version 1.4.11.4 changed starter-pack variables. Updating from 1.4.11.2 or earlier may replace items in affected inventory slots when the Starter Pack gamerule is enabled.\n\nCHANGELOG\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n- Introduced Zombified Skeleton, Zombified Spider, and Zombified Creeper.\n- Expanded cooking, ingredients, crops, monster drops, and status-effect descriptions.\n- Added glowing textures to radiated and zombified monsters.\n\nNEW ENTITIES AND COMBAT\n- Added Zombified Skeleton, Zombified Spider, and Zombified Creeper.\n- Added conditional glow rendering for Zombified Spider and Zombified Creeper, including an exploding appearance for the Creeper.\n- Added a Zombified Creeper explosion system, an explosion display condition, and synchronized CTF variable/counter logic.\n- Updated the Zombified Skeleton renderer and Zombified Creeper explosion behavior and display.\n- Updated targeting for Electro, Powered Electric Soldier, Electric Soldiers, Ice Soldiers, and Wendigo Stage 1.\n- Expanded Zombie Infection handling for Electro variants, Electric and Ice units, animals, and vanilla mobs.\n- Updated immunity handling for new zombified entities, including Instant Death immunity and monster-immunity logic.\n\nBLOCKS, PLANTS, FOOD, AND ITEMS\n- Added Rock Salt Block, its loot table, and the Salt ingredient.\n- Added Black Pepper Plant, Peppercorn, and Black Pepper, including plant loot and a Black Pepper recipe.\n- Added Raw Squid, Cooked Squid, Rotten Mutton, and Rotten Porkchop.\n- Added Salami, Cooked Salami, and Mozzarella Cheese.\n- Added Knife and Bowl of Fruit Salad.\n- Added Infected Bone, Infected Spider Eye, and Infected Gunpowder as monster drops/ingredients.\n- Added loot drops for Zombified Skeleton, Zombified Spider, Zombified Creeper, Zombified Sheep, and Zombified Pig.\n\nRECIPES AND RECIPE UNLOCKS\n- Added cooked Squid and cooked Salami smelting recipes and unlockers.\n- Added Mozzarella Cheese, Salami, Knife, Black Pepper, and Fruit Salad recipes and unlockers.\n- Added ingredient tags for fruits, sweeteners, flowers, and zombies.\n\nFOOD, THIRST, AND STATUS EFFECTS\n- Added written descriptions for status effects.\n- Updated food replenishment and draining for Beetroot, Glow Berries, Squid, Chorus Fruit, and Mozzarella Cheese.\n- Integrated ETD into PTB food/drink replenishment and draining, including fruit, crop, and vegetable handling.\n- Adjusted Sushi food properties and the Infected Spider Eye's eating behavior.\n- Updated Fuse status effect behavior with respect to mob griefing.\n\nVISUALS, MUSIC, AND SYSTEMS\n- Added a glow texture for Radiated Zombie and new glow/explosion visuals for zombified mobs.\n- Updated ambient and automatic music playback and the Bossbar Executable system.\n- Adjusted Restrict Sun Burn and monster targeting systems.\n\nBUG FIXES\n- Fixed the Mild Decay exhaustion applier.\n- Fixed the Fatigue exhaustion applier.",
